+# Summary
+
+**Changed**
+- `stockreport/report.py`: added a `markdown` format to `render()`. It uses the project's vendored `tabulate` with `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`. The table is followed by a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown` as well as `text`.
+
+**Verified**
+- Before the change, `python -m unittest` had 1 failure and 1 error, both from the missing markdown format.
+- After the change, `python -W error -m unittest` ran 3 tests and all passed. That covers the text output, the markdown output and the CLI markdown run. `-W error` turns warnings into errors, so no deprecated tabulate keywords are in use.
+
+**Not verified / notes**
+- I only checked against `inventory.csv`, through the existing tests.
+- I did not edit the vendored `tabulate` or any tests.
+- The markdown output does not escape `|` characters in item names. The sample data has none.
